    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_b1_opinions_reasons_opinion_frames",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "b1-opinions-reasons-01",
        "slug": "b1-opinions-reasons-opinion-frames",
        "title": "Developing an opinion",
        "rule_summary": "Use frames such as In my view, The main reason is…, and For example… to structure an opinion clearly.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای ساختار دادن نظر از عباراتی مثل In my view، The main reason is و For example استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "In my view, the change is positive.",
            "fa": "از نظر من این تغییر مثبته."
          },
          {
            "en": "The main reason is cost.",
            "fa": "دلیل اصلی هزینه است."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "B1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_b1_opinions_reasons_reason_links",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "b1-opinions-reasons-02",
        "slug": "b1-opinions-reasons-reason-links",
        "title": "because / since / as",
        "rule_summary": "Use because, since, or as to connect a claim with a reason; because is usually the most direct.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای وصل کردن ادعا و دلیل از because، since یا as استفاده می‌کنیم؛ because مستقیم‌تر است."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "I prefer the train because it's more reliable.",
            "fa": "قطار رو ترجیح می‌دم چون قابل‌اعتمادتره."
          },
          {
            "en": "Since we have time, let's compare both options.",
            "fa": "چون وقت داریم، هر دو گزینه رو مقایسه کنیم."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "B1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_b1_opinions_reasons_concession",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "b1-opinions-reasons-03",
        "slug": "b1-opinions-reasons-concession",
        "title": "although / even though",
        "rule_summary": "Use although or even though to acknowledge a contrasting fact before keeping your main position.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با although یا even though یک نکته مخالف رو می‌پذیریم ولی موضع اصلی رو حفظ می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
